{
  "configuration_id": "config_029",
  "reason": "The current best (config_023: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted, acc=0.713) shows a clear ~0.06 advantage over the matching rna_only transformer setup (config_001, acc=0.653), indicating the image modality is contributing meaningfully. However, all experiments so far have used ResNet50 as the image encoder. config_029 swaps only the image encoder to imagenet_vit_l while keeping the proven multiprofile + transformer + weighted pipeline intact. This single-variable change directly tests whether a stronger, more expressive image representation can amplify the multimodal gain, which is the largest unexplored design axis with high potential impact. It is more informative than testing fusion (weighted vs concat) because the image encoder is a fundamental representation bottleneck, and a positive result would justify further investment in image-side improvements, while a null result would confirm ResNet50 is sufficient and redirect effort to RNA encoder or fusion choices."
}

